    "mentat/app/evidence-csv.js:loadRows (SELECT)",
    "mentat/app/evidence-csv.js: sources listing render + #evidence-csv-source population",
    "mentat/app/evidence-csv.js: pre-flight size check against LIMITS"
  ],
  "description": "The shapes read once a CSV has been imported: the size/row/column LIMITS the client pre-flights against, one imported CSV's CATALOG (nested inside a sources listing or a SELECT), the GET /api/evidence-csv sources listing, a paginated SELECT of one committee/cycle's rows, and the bounded error-payload shape (never a leaked Python exception string). Orientation only - the examples are the contract. v3 (S7, 2026-09-17): every committee carries the category the file gave it or the FEC committee master inferred, with the source of that label; the CATALOG carries the per-category rollup the picker filters on, its excluded-row count and the CATALOG_VERSION its rules were built under, plus the three fields that say whether this console is re-reading the import; the SELECT carries the rows the workbook excluded from its own analysis.",
